p("socrates","Socrates","ソクラテス",-470,-399,["gr"],["philosophy"],"Socrates was an ancient Greek philosopher credited as the founder of Western philosophy. He developed the Socratic method of questioning to stimulate critical thinking.","Socrates was born in Athens. His father was a stonemason and his mother a midwife. He served in the Athenian military and later devoted himself entirely to philosophical inquiry.","Socrates' method of dialectical questioning became the foundation of Western philosophical inquiry. His emphasis on ethics, self-knowledge, and reasoned argument transformed intellectual life.",[(-432,"Served in the Peloponnesian War"),(-423,"Depicted in Aristophanes' The Clouds"),(-399,"Tried and executed for impiety and corrupting youth")],[("Socratic Method",-400,"Dialectical method of inquiry using questions to stimulate critical thinking")],[("The unexamined life is not worth living.","Plato, Apology")])

p("plato","Plato","プラトン",-428,-348,["gr"],["philosophy"],"Plato was an ancient Greek philosopher who founded the Academy in Athens, the first institution of higher learning in the Western world. His philosophical writings have shaped Western thought for millennia.","Plato was born into an aristocratic Athenian family. He became a student of Socrates and was profoundly affected by his teacher's execution in 399 BC.","Plato's theory of Forms, his political philosophy in the Republic, and his dialogues established the framework for Western metaphysics, epistemology, and political thought.",[(-399,"Witnessed the execution of Socrates"),(-387,"Founded the Academy in Athens"),(-380,"Wrote The Republic"),(-360,"Wrote Timaeus and later dialogues")],[("The Republic",-380,"Philosophical work on justice, the ideal state, and the theory of Forms"),("Symposium",-385,"Dialogue on the nature of love and beauty")],[("Be kind, for everyone you meet is fighting a hard battle.","Attributed")])

p("aristotle","Aristotle","アリストテレス",-384,-322,["gr"],["philosophy","biology"],"Aristotle was an ancient Greek philosopher and polymath whose writings cover physics, biology, metaphysics, logic, ethics, and politics. He was Plato's student and Alexander the Great's tutor.","Aristotle was born in Stagira, Chalcidice. He joined Plato's Academy at age 17 and remained there for 20 years before founding his own school, the Lyceum.","Aristotle's systematic approach to knowledge created the foundation for Western science and philosophy. His logic dominated for two millennia, and his works on ethics and politics remain studied today.",[(-367,"Joined Plato's Academy"),(-343,"Became tutor to Alexander the Great"),(-335,"Founded the Lyceum in Athens"),(-322,"Fled Athens and died in Chalcis")],[("Nicomachean Ethics",-340,"Foundational work on virtue ethics and the good life"),("Politics",-330,"Analysis of political systems and the ideal state"),("Organon",-350,"Collection of works on logic that defined the field for centuries")],[("Knowing yourself is the beginning of all wisdom.","Attributed")])

