p("ludwig-wittgenstein","Ludwig Wittgenstein","ルートヴィヒ・ウィトゲンシュタイン",1889,1951,["at","gb"],["philosophy"],"Ludwig Wittgenstein was an Austrian-British philosopher who made revolutionary contributions to logic, philosophy of language, and philosophy of mind. He is considered one of the greatest philosophers of the 20th century.","Wittgenstein was born in Vienna into one of Europe's wealthiest families. He studied engineering before turning to philosophy under Bertrand Russell at Cambridge.","Wittgenstein's two major works represent two distinct philosophical approaches: the logical atomism of the Tractatus and the language-game theory of the Investigations. Both transformed analytic philosophy.",[(1921,"Published Tractatus Logico-Philosophicus"),(1929,"Returned to Cambridge"),(1939,"Succeeded G.E. Moore as professor at Cambridge"),(1953,"Philosophical Investigations published posthumously")],[("Tractatus Logico-Philosophicus",1921,"Logical analysis of the relationship between language and reality"),("Philosophical Investigations",1953,"Rejected earlier work, introduced language games and family resemblance")],[("Whereof one cannot speak, thereof one must be silent.","Tractatus Logico-Philosophicus, 1921")])

